  "label": "Ableist Stereotype",
  "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that physical disability inherently limits one's capacity for emotional or physical support, which is a harmful ableist trope. This stereotype implies that only able-bodied individuals can meaningfully 'stand by' someone, reinforcing the idea that disability equates to incapacity in supportive roles.",
